      "title": "Inspect Explorer Scope",
      "type": "text",
      "description": "Scope banner for the selected-range Silver reject explorer. This dashboard covers only Silver FILTERED_OUT_SILVER quarantine-backed rows; DQ quarantine, skipped records, warning/nullification, and Gold validation failures belong in Data Quality. A zero-reject workflow run can legitimately produce 0 totals and empty record tables, but only after one concrete pipeline, a responding Quarantine Explorer, and a valid Bronze denominator are confirmed."
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "content": "<div style='padding:0.6rem 0.8rem;line-height:1.55'><strong>First action:</strong> if total rejects are non-zero, inspect top reason/field/signature, open a payload_hash drilldown from the table, then decide whether to fix transformer logic, schema/DQ rule configuration, provider drift, or replay/resolve via quarantine CLI. <strong>No-data:</strong> a zero-reject workflow run is an intentional empty explorer state only when Quarantine Explorer responds, one concrete pipeline is selected, and Bronze records are present. Zero matching rows for the active filters is an empty result, not a datasource failure; datasource/plugin errors, unsupported filter chains, unknown pipeline, or bronze_records=0 are UNKNOWN or error states until the backend is checked. <strong>Lineage:</strong> use run_id and batch/Bronze evidence where available before replay decisions. <a href='https://github.com/SatoryKono/BioactivityDataAcquisition/blob/main/docs/05-operations/runbooks/quarantine-management.md' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener'>Open Quarantine Management Runbook</a>.</div>",
        "mode": "html"
